 {
  "source": "Deutsche Bank",
  "title": "Workday: Post-Rising Thoughts: Building the Agentic Growth Engine",
  "type": "equity_research",
  "priority": "medium",
  "published": "2026-10-19",
  "insights": [
   "Deutsche Bank maintains a Hold rating on Workday following the Rising event and Financial Analyst Day, noting that while the company's agentic AI strategy is sound, investors are likely to wait for tangible financial impact before rewarding the stock.",
   "Workday reiterated its initial FY28 outlook of ~11% y/y subscription revenue growth and 33%+ non-GAAP operating margins.",
   "Agentic offerings are a key growth driver, expected to represent >50% of incremental customer expansion ARR this year and stepping up to ~70% next year.",
   "The acquisition of C1.ai is seen as a logical tuck-in to expand Workday's identity governance and IT presence, though there is uncertainty regarding whether large enterprises will adopt identity offerings from Workday over traditional cybersecurity vendors.",
   "Customer expansion remains the fastest route to revenue, representing ~60% of TTM subscription revenue growth.",
   "Workday is seeing traction in the Medium Enterprise segment (500-3,500 employees), with net new deal sizes increasing 20% y/y.",
   "Product attach rates show mixed results: Talent Optimization (67%) and Planning (46%) are strong, while Core Financials (37%) and Extend (y/y decline) show some deceleration concerns.",
   "Workday now has $600mn in agentic AI ARR, more than 3x from last year."
  ],
  "market_movers": [
   {
    "ticker": "WDAY",
    "action": "reiterate",
    "rating": "Hold",
    "price_target": "$220.00",
    "rationale": "Investors are likely to wait to see tangible evidence of financial impact from agentic AI initiatives before rewarding shares.",
    "conviction": "medium"
   }
  ],
